ALGORITHM: Reverse Nodes in k-Group

1. Start.

2. Check whether there are at least k nodes
   starting from the current head.

3. If fewer than k nodes are available:
       Return head.
       Do not reverse the remaining nodes.

4. Initialize:
       prev = NULL
       cur = head

5. Reverse exactly k nodes:

       Repeat k times:
           next = cur.next
           cur.next = prev
           prev = cur
           cur = next

6. After reversing:
       prev = new head of the current group
       head = last node of the current group

7. Recursively reverse the remaining nodes:
       head.next = reverseKGroup(cur, k)

8. Return prev.

9. Continue until the complete linked list
   has been processed.

TIME COMPLEXITY:
O(n)

SPACE COMPLEXITY:
O(n/k) due to recursion.
